cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CuMIN: Curated ROIs for Minian"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Fung"
    given-names: "Sam"
    affiliation: "Leslie Dan Faculty of Pharmacy, University of Toronto"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # <- add yours
  # - family-names: ""
  #   given-names: ""
  #   affiliation: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/samwcfung/CuMIN"
abstract: >-
  A modular pipeline for extracting and analysing calcium fluorescence traces
  from manually curated ROIs in spinal dorsal horn slice recordings. Applies
  photobleaching correction, background removal and denoising, extracts per-ROI
  dF/F traces, detects events, and produces per-slice, per-mouse and
  per-pain-model summaries.
keywords:
  - calcium imaging
  - spinal cord
  - dorsal horn
  - chronic pain
  - ROI analysis
license: MIT          # <- change if you choose a different licence
version: "1.0.0"      # <- bump per release
date-released: "2026-07-23"   # <- update on release

